# Drive the rover to a target position, avoiding obstacles on the way.
#
# The three sections below are what separates an action from a service. A
# service has only the first and second (request/response); the third — feedback
# streamed while the work is still running — and the ability to cancel a goal in
# flight are what make an action the right fit for a task that takes time.

# --- Goal: what the caller asks for (R1) -------------------------------------
geometry_msgs/Point target      # target position in the reference frame
float64 tolerance               # arrival radius; <= 0 uses the node's default
---
# --- Result: how it ended (R4, R7) -------------------------------------------
bool success
string message                  # human-readable outcome, e.g. why it aborted
float64 final_distance_error    # how far from the target it actually stopped
geometry_msgs/Point final_position
---
# --- Feedback: published while driving (R6) ----------------------------------
float64 distance_remaining
float64 heading_error_deg
geometry_msgs/Point current_position
string state                    # DRIVING | TURNING | AVOIDING | CLEARING
